    No game execution; engine separation and final acceptance remain open.

Phase 3: Migrate existing scopes and liquid input translation
  Depends on Phase 2. Outcome: VGE use/restoration and liquid input staging no longer need an engine owner.
  Proposal: Existing scope ownership and engine handoff; Liquid mesh-pool input bridge.

  ☑ Consolidate graphics/compute restoration within existing program scopes and command lifetimes.
    - Replace CurrentShaderProgram-based VGE capture and compute numeric-ID owner lookup with
      borrowed IGpuProgram/generation references carried only where the existing scopes need them.
    - Preserve GraphicsCommandContext ShaderActivation, pipeline-change/EndPass cleanup and
      EngineBoundaryScope exceptional cleanup; do not duplicate selected-pipeline ownership.
    - Validate context, revision and retirement before restoration; stale tokens must not unbind
      another owner or restore a recycled handle. Extend existing scopes only as required.
    - Restore input resources where immediate scopes promise it; otherwise preserve explicit
      next-draw submission. Avoid redundant replay across complete resource-restoring boundaries.
    - Route direct Use/TryUse/UseScope and low-level compute paths through their declared scope
      contract; retain standalone/headless operation without a game singleton.
  ☑ Move native shader capture/Stop/Use to Rendering/Integration at supported outer boundaries.
    - Include native restoration effects in the footprint and ordered cleanup; preserve rejection
      of unsupported native/raw/compute incoming states and targeted StateCache mutation semantics.
  ☑ Implement the chosen narrow MeshDataPoolManager input bridge during LiquidGraphicsSubmission.
    - Translate origin, modelViewMatrix and forcedTransparency into the typed liquid input sink.
      Preserve engine culling, dimension offsets, interpolation, visibility and finally writes.
    - Keep pool draws on GraphicsCommandContext.Draw and borrowed geometry lifetime/validation
      with EngineLiquidPoolGeometry and LiquidGraphicsSubmission.
    - Native pool rendering must still receive the native shader; handle unknown inputs explicitly.
      No global CurrentActiveShader patch or engine executable proxy. An input-only adapter must
      reject unsupported executable operations and never enter engine registry/current-owner state.
  ☑ Validate all graphics/compute nesting combinations, unchanged-ID submission, success/failure,
    exceptional cleanup, resource restoration, raw bindings, disposal and context/ID reuse.
  ☑ Validate visible/depth liquids for ordinary, empty/culled pools, dimension offsets,
    mini-dimension transforms, preview transparency, restoration writes and exceptions; include
    unrelated native pools and real engine traversal where feasible.
  ☑ Completion: boundary and liquid checks pass; VGE scope behavior is independent of engine owner
    state, with native handoff contained in integration. Remove temporary scope compatibility paths.

