Phase 4: Remove engine executable inheritance and registration
  Depends on Phase 3. Outcome: independent VGE executables prepare and render on cached/uncached paths.
  Proposal: Executable preparation and retirement; Proposed ownership model; Compatibility.

  ☑ Remove ShaderProgram/ShaderProgramBase inheritance and IShaderProgram from VGE executable owners.
    - Remove engine Shader creation, stage slots, EngineDisposed reflection, PassId and inherited
      uniformLocations requirements. Keep useful GpuProgramInterface diagnostic projections.
    - Remove RegisterOnPreparation/RegisterMemoryShaderProgram coupling and transition paths.
    - Move liquid interface methods fully into the bridge; migrate remaining uniform/texture
      consumers and fixtures to generated properties or preparation-owned numeric helpers.
  ☑ Compose graphics executable ownership through GpuProgramObject.Adopt and GpuResource policy.
    - Prepare/validate candidates before publishing executable, layout, installed settings,
      graphics identity, asset generation and successful revision together.
    - Retain the previous generation after failure/superseded requests without claiming readiness
      for incompatible requests; reject stale GraphicsPipeline borrowers after replacement.
    - Preserve ShaderLinkBatch, SPIR-V loader, binary cache, numeric bindings and desired inputs.
    - Update PendingShaderProgram transfers for synchronous, batch, failed and cancelled paths;
      detach/release temporary stages once after successful linking. Cached programs need no stages.
    - Use StateCache.DeleteProgram/targeted resource retirement; reject or defer active borrowing
      according to the chosen policy. Keep terminal disposal distinct from executable invalidation.
  ☑ Expose preparation diagnostics so mandatory HDR failure identifies the program and real cause.
  ☑ Remove obsolete OwnedShaderSubmissionHook/GpuProgramStopHook behavior after explicit frame/light
    bindings are verified; reconcile SceneColorProgramBindings, LiquidPoolSubmissionHook and
    EngineBoundaryExecution type checks. Preserve native-only hooks and profiling labels via adapters.
  ☑ Validate pbr_final from a real executable-cache hit with no NewShader or engine registration;
    repeat cache miss, invalid-cache fallback, batched load and preparation failure.
    - Test replacement failure/supersession, monotonic successful revisions, cancellation and
      exactly-once stage/program retirement. Fixtures must reject accidental engine registration.
  ☑ Completion: structural checks and focused GPU evidence show independent cached/uncached rendering,
    no engine executable assignability/registration, and no stale engine-specific VGE hooks remain.
    Reload/shutdown completion in Phase 5 is required before release.

  Traceability: executable separation -> proposal Proposed ownership model and Compatibility ->
