Phase 5: Establish registry, reload and context lifetime
  Depends on Phase 4. Outcome: VGE ownership remains correct across assets, worlds and context retirement.
  Proposal: Concrete registry responsibilities; Reload and lifecycle sequencing.

  ☑ Make GpuShaderPrograms an instance owned by client rendering lifetime with explicit composition.
    - Decouple core identity from ICoreClientAPI; preserve typed lookup and useful mismatch diagnostics.
    - Enforce the selected duplicate-declaration policy without silently discarding incompatible
      types/contracts/settings or constructing throwaway replacement owners on asset reload.
    - Keep declarations/lookup free of binary reads and GL work; selected preload follows configuration.
      Preserve demand preparation, failed-input suppression and observable readiness/failure details.
    - Own removal, shutdown and callback invalidation so retired worlds/registries cannot revive.
  ☑ Adapt assets/logging through ShaderAssetReader, digest access and diagnostic sinks at integration.
    - Include ShaderLinkBatch's engine asset-manager boundary; preserve shared source identity and
      asset generation without duplicating import/digest/binary-cache services.
  ☑ Replace delayed RegisterAll invalidation with a synchronous reload transaction.
    - At a safe boundary withdraw old readiness, mark reload, clear digest/import caches and capture
      coherent settings. Let the engine refresh/rebuild native shaders before completing VGE invalidation.
    - Withdraw dependent render publications, reopen demand preparation and preload only selected
      mandatory sets when configured. Handle native exceptions, suppressed reload and compile failure.
    - Report native API reload status separately from VGE lazy/mandatory readiness; eliminate any
      window where old assets appear current because a callback has not executed yet.
  ☑ Apply the chosen compute reload policy to feature owners and test successful-executable reload.
    - Preserve CPU input state required by the policy; do not treat failure retry as executable reload.
  ☑ Wire actual shutdown order: stop submissions, dispose renderer/PSO borrowers, retire registry
    programs and drain native deletion on the live originating context.
    - Keep configuration, asset reload, world leave/re-entry and native context retirement distinct.
      Withdraw owner knowledge before context reuse; abandon deletion with a destroyed context
      rather than delete a matching numeric handle on another context.
  ☑ Validate duplicate/mismatched declarations, demand/preload failures, reload ordering/failures,
    settings edits, feature compute reload, world re-entry, queued callbacks and retired-context reuse.
    - Prove CPU blocks survive executable reload and retire once; verify targeted cache deletion.
  ☑ Completion: no delayed registration dependency remains; lifecycle checks establish coherent
    readiness, no owner resurrection and correct borrower/resource retirement ordering.

