  Live rejection: the user reported the sun follows camera motion and shadows follow screen-center
    aiming after the early publication change. The 119-test selection proved internal snapshot
    consistency and reuse, not equivalence with the established Opaque camera data. Global camera
    capture has been restored to its original Opaque implementation; the associated early-publication
    regression was withdrawn. The archived correction above is superseded and must not be treated
    as accepted. Liquid-depth availability and permanent failure handling require further diagnosis.
    Installed engine IL subsequently identified the concrete corruption: CurrentProjectionMatrix
    and CurrentModelViewMatrix return the same mutable tmpMatrix array. The rejected early publisher
    retained a view span, then read projection and overwrote that view. Separate mock arrays concealed
    the defect. The restored Opaque publisher uses the independent CameraMatrixOriginf storage.

